e consideration, ascertain what is proper or improper; persons of your vast wisdom are cognizant of the right or wrong by dint of their understanding.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-66-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3062015","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"821cb1e556b666a378054321524cf5b412bf66cbd75c113f7bff7b16b2fab8a6","compact":"c18d79c89872d51adb7c42b123cb4222102131da794ebee03b4d0663e24cd4bc","nasal":"d68134c96802cd4720e07162c20d7303701d8997aaf357a9bf4f2894a665a427"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-62-16","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":62,"verse":16,"english":"Without proper exercise, actions, of unknown merit and uncertain issue do not bear fruits.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.629,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-66-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3062016","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3651c88f82f7c21470d8f852fdb06f3066784a68d3c02282a1de29a0be457d2d","compact":"b0e7adda7cec7d0b9b58c63471757ded78a743f2136f27002bab73c58ff48991","nasal":"5dcabd3b8a7b16433677d52b45909617ff49220fc66575eb7dfa56a3f49e2d7b"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-62-17","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":62,"verse":17,"english":"O hero, many a time and oft ere this, you had given me the self-same counsel. Who is capable of counselling you who are the very preceptor of the gods?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.692,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-66-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3062017","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"234228f9581bc7625921f6c815a250546754637379d83834977811829e2f90ff","compact":"b4eb332a0b116df41b665226ebfe7baf7cbfd54dfa26051691ce0d871d0a867c","nasal":"b4eb332a0b116df41b665226ebfe7baf7cbfd54dfa2605